lor:`#1F2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},children:`}`})}),`\n`]})})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The client `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`SHOULD`}),` select a mutually supported version from the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`supported`}),`\nlist and retry the request, or surface an error to the user if no compatible\nversion exists.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Servers `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`MUST`}),` implement\n`,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/specification/2026-07-28/server/discover`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`server/discover`})}),`. Clients\n`,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`MAY`}),` call it before sending any other requests to learn the server’s\nsupported versions up front, but are not required to: a client is free to\ninvoke any RPC inline and handle `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`UnsupportedProtocolVersionError`}),` if its\npreferred version is not supported.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`extension-negotiation`,children:`Extension Negotiation`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Clients and servers can negotiate support for optional\n`,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/extensions/overview`,children:`extensions`}),` beyond the core protocol. Extensions\nare advertised in the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`extensions`}),` field of capabilities, which is a map of\nextension identifiers to per-extension settings objects. Extension identifiers\n`,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`MUST`}),` follow the `,_jsxs(_components.a,{href:`/specification/2026-07-28/basic/index#_meta`,children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`_meta`}),` key naming rules`]}),`,\nwith a mandatory prefix.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The following is an example of a client that advertises the\n`,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/extensions/apps/overview`,children:`MCP Apps extension`}),` identified as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`io.modelcontextprotocol/ui`}),`:`]}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLin