dshake) and `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#terminology`,children:`modern`}),` clients (which\nuse per-request metadata) `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`MAY`}),` implement both behaviors.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`A client that needs to interoperate with both kinds of servers detects the\nserver’s era with transport-specific mechanics, specified in the binding\npages:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio#backward-compatibility`,children:`stdio`}),`:\nprobe with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`server/discover`}),` and fall back on any error that is not a\nrecognized modern error.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http#backward-compatibility`,children:`Streamable HTTP`}),`:\nattempt a modern request and inspect the body of a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`400 Bad Request`}),`\nbefore falling back.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`In both cases, a recognized modern JSON-RPC error (such as\n`,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/specification/2026-07-28/schema#unsupportedprotocolversionerror`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`UnsupportedProtocolVersionError`})}),`)\nidentifies a modern server: the client retries with a supported version\nrather than falling back. Anything else identifies a legacy server.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The era determination is a property of the server, not of an individual\nrequest. Clients `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`SHOULD`}),` cache the result for the lifetime of the server\nprocess (stdio) or origin (HTTP), and `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`MAY`}),` persist it across restarts of\nthe same server configuration, re-probing if the cached assumption later\nfails.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A server that supports only `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#terminology`,children:`modern`}),` versions `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`SHOULD`}),` name\nthe protocol versions it supports in any error it returns to an `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`initialize`}),`\nrequest, on any transport: legacy clients have no fall-forward mechanism, and\nthis message may be the only diagnostic they can surface to users.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`compatibility-matrix`,children:`Compatibility Matrix`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`The following matrix summarizes the expected outcome of every combination of\nclient and server era:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Client`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Server`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Outcome`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Modern`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Modern`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Works. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`server/discover`}),` is optional; version mismatches surface as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`UnsupportedProtocolVersionError`}),` and the client retries with a mutually supported version.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Modern`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Legacy`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Fails. The server may reject the request with an implementation-defined error, stay silent, or even process an era-ambiguous method under legacy semantics. On stdio, clients `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`SHOULD`}),` send `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`server/discover`}),` first to fail deterministically; the client then surfaces an actionable error to the user.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Modern`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Dual-era`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Works. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`server/discover`}),` is optional; version mismatches surface as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`UnsupportedProtocolVersionError`}),` and the client retries with a mutually supported version. The server serves the client statelessly according to that version.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Dual-era`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Modern`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Works. The stdio probe returns a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`DiscoverResult`}),` (or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`UnsupportedProtocolVersionError`}),`); on HTTP, the first modern request succeeds or returns a modern error. The client stays modern.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Dual-era`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Legacy`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Works. stdio: the probe returns a non-modern error or times out, and the client falls back to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`initialize`}),`. HTTP: the modern request returns a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`4xx`}),` without a recognized modern error body, and the client falls back to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`initialize`}),` (and possibly further to the deprecated HTTP+SSE transport).`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Dual-era`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Dual-era`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Works. The stdio probe returns a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`DiscoverResult`}),` (or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`UnsupportedProtocolVersionError`}),`); on HTTP, the first modern request succeeds or returns a modern error. If there is a mutually supported modern version, the client stays modern.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Legacy`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Modern`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Fails. stdio: the server rejects `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`initialize`}),` with a JSON-RPC error; the exact code is implementation-defined (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`initialize`}),` is an unknown method and the request also lacks the required `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`_meta`}),` fields). HTTP: the request is missing the required headers and is rejected per `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http#server-validation`,children:`server validation`}),` with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`400 Bad Request`}),` (a client on the deprecated HTTP+SSE transport fails at its opening `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET`}),` instead). Legacy clients have no fall-forward mechanism.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Legacy`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Dual-era`}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Works. The server answers `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`initialize`}),` and serves the client according to the negotiated legacy revision.`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Legacy`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Legacy`}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Works according to the legacy revision; out of scope for this document.`})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A dual-era `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`server`}),` selects its behavior from how the client opens:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`A request carrying modern per-request `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`_meta`}),` is served statelessly\naccording to this revision.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`An `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`initialize`}),` request selects legacy semantics, scoped to the stdio\nprocess (stdio) or the session (HTTP), as specified by the negotiated\nlegacy protocol version.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A dual-era server `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`MAY`}),` serve both eras concurrently on the same endpoint\nor process.`]})]})}function MDXContent(props={}){const{wrapper:MDXLayout}={..._provideComponents(),...props.components};return MDXLayou